From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 17:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] keyboard: Keys typed while the focus moves reach the new window

Switching to another window and typing at once lost the first letters.
Mutter names the focused window at once, but the keyboard focus reaches
the client later: the surface takes it on the compositor's next focus
update, and the client is told then. Measured on a headless session, the
window focus changed 1 ms after the switch while the client was told
between 4 ms and 5.5 s later, and a key typed in between went to the
window being left, or nowhere at all -- the letters the person watched
disappear.

The keys typed during a handover between two client windows are now
held and given to the window the focus is going to as soon as it has it,
in the order they were typed and with their own times. A key still held
down when the focus lands is already named in the enter event, so only
its release is sent on; a release whose press the previous window had
goes to that window, so no client is left with a key it thinks is down.

Nothing is ever held while the shell has the keyboard: a grab or modal,
the lock screen and its unlock dialog, the overview search, the run
dialog, or any shell actor with the key focus. Those keys go to the shell
at once. A grab starting or ending ends a handover on the spot, and a
handover that never lands hands its keys, in order, to whoever has the
keyboard after a second -- the shell included. No key is ever dropped:
dropping them on a timeout left the lock screen unable to take a
password after waking, because the focus there is the shell's own and a
handover towards a window never completed.

The rules live in meta-key-handover.c, apart from the rest of Mutter, and
are tested by src/tests/key-handover-test.c in %check.

MUTTER_DEBUG_KEY_HANDOVER=1 logs every key with where it went, every
keyboard focus change, and the keys the shell keeps for itself, which is
how the handover was measured.

---
diff --git a/src/core/display.c b/src/core/display.c
index 94b4cb8..de0b039 100644
--- a/src/core/display.c
+++ b/src/core/display.c
@@ -1149,6 +1149,17 @@ on_is_grabbed_changed (ClutterStage *stage,
 {
   MetaDisplayPrivate *priv = meta_display_get_instance_private (display);
 
+  /* Luma: a grab starting or ending (a modal, the lock screen, the
+   * overview) ends any keyboard focus handover at once. Keys held for it go
+   * to whoever has the keyboard now, the shell included; none are dropped. */
+  {
+    MetaWaylandCompositor *compositor = wayland_compositor_from_display (display);
+
+    if (compositor)
+      meta_wayland_compositor_release_held_keys (compositor,
+                                                 "the shell took or gave back the keyboard");
+  }
+
   if (!priv->focus_on_grab_dismissed.window)
     return;
 
diff --git a/src/core/events.c b/src/core/events.c
index b4bf668..683599a 100644
--- a/src/core/events.c
+++ b/src/core/events.c
@@ -263,13 +263,32 @@ meta_display_handle_event (MetaDisplay        *display,
       meta_keybindings_process_event (display, window, event))
     return CLUTTER_EVENT_STOP;
 
+  /* Luma: a key typed while the keyboard moves from one client window to
+   * another is held for the new window. Nothing is held while the shell has
+   * the keyboard (a grab, a modal, the lock screen, an entry with the key
+   * focus); a key that is not held first lets any held keys go, in order,
+   * to whoever has the keyboard. See meta-key-handover.c.
+   */
+  if (IS_KEY_EVENT (event_type) &&
+      meta_wayland_compositor_maybe_hold_key (wayland_compositor, event))
+    return CLUTTER_EVENT_STOP;
+
   /* Do not pass keyboard events to Wayland if key focus is not on the
    * stage in normal mode (e.g. during keynav in the panel)
    */
   if (!has_grab)
     {
       if (IS_KEY_EVENT (event_type) && !stage_has_key_focus (display))
-        return CLUTTER_EVENT_PROPAGATE;
+        {
+          /* Luma: measuring where a key goes during a handover. */
+          if (g_getenv ("MUTTER_DEBUG_KEY_HANDOVER"))
+            {
+              g_message ("[luma-keys] key event kept by the shell, which "
+                         "holds the key focus, at %" G_GINT64_FORMAT " us",
+                         g_get_monotonic_time ());
+            }
+          return CLUTTER_EVENT_PROPAGATE;
+        }
     }
 
   if (event_type == CLUTTER_SCROLL &&
@@ -286,7 +305,14 @@ meta_display_handle_event (MetaDisplay        *display,
     return CLUTTER_EVENT_PROPAGATE;
 
   if (stage_has_grab (display))
-    return CLUTTER_EVENT_PROPAGATE;
+    {
+      if (IS_KEY_EVENT (event_type) && g_getenv ("MUTTER_DEBUG_KEY_HANDOVER"))
+        {
+          g_message ("[luma-keys] key event kept by a shell grab at %"
+                     G_GINT64_FORMAT " us", g_get_monotonic_time ());
+        }
+      return CLUTTER_EVENT_PROPAGATE;
+    }
 
   if (window)
     {
diff --git a/src/meson.build b/src/meson.build
index 80b48bc..fb34150 100644
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -583,6 +583,8 @@ mutter_sources += [
